# Mytheus ingress. Owned by THIS repo, served by a Caddy this repo does not own.
#
# The box runs one Caddy (the atithivishram-prod stack). It holds 80/443, and cf-origin-lock
# admits Cloudflare traffic only to those ports, so a second TLS terminator is not possible.
# For a while the Mytheus site blocks therefore lived inside that other product's Caddyfile,
# which meant changing Mytheus routing meant editing atithivishram-infra, and a Mytheus deploy
# could not change its own ingress.
#
# This file is the decoupling. atithivishram-infra carries one permanent line -
# `import /etc/caddy/conf.d/*.caddy` - plus a read-only mount of /srv/mytheus/caddy/conf.d.
# Everything Mytheus-specific lives here and is deployed by mytheus-deploy.sh.
#
# Two constraints this file must respect, because breaking either takes down a product that
# is not ours:
#
#   1. It is spliced into another product's config. A syntax error here fails validation of
#      the WHOLE Caddyfile, Atithi's five domains included. mytheus-deploy.sh therefore runs
#      `caddy validate` and refuses to reload if this file does not parse.
#   2. Only ever define mytheus.cloud site blocks here. A block for a hostname this repo does
#      not own would silently take over that hostname from its real definition.
#
# `tls internal` rather than an ACME certificate: cf-origin-lock drops non-Cloudflare ingress
# on 80, so an HTTP-01 challenge can never complete. This requires the mytheus.cloud zone to
# stay on Cloudflare SSL mode Full; Full (strict) rejects an internally-issued cert.

# The web application: marketing at /, the authenticated shell at /dashboard and below, the
# meeting room under /meetings. One Next.js app with route groups (doc 20 section 2.2), so the
# marketing site is a path inside it and not a separate origin. Both the apex and www are
# served rather than one redirecting to the other, because Clerk session cookies are scoped to
# the host that set them and bouncing between the two mid-flow drops the session.
mytheus.cloud, www.mytheus.cloud {
	encode zstd gzip
	# `mytheus-webapp`, not `ui`. This Caddy is attached to both stacks' networks and
	# atithivishram-prod also has a container aliased `ui`, so the bare name resolved to THEIR
	# container and this host served their product. Any upstream named here must be unique
	# across every network this Caddy is on.
	reverse_proxy mytheus-webapp:3000
	tls internal
}

vps.mytheus.cloud {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy dokploy:3000
	tls internal
}

api.mytheus.cloud {
	encode zstd gzip
	# api-gateway, not core-api directly. The gateway pre-validates the Clerk token, resolves
	# the tenant once, and FAILS CLOSED before any tenant-scoped store is touched; pointing
	# this at a service bypasses that checkpoint entirely. It also owns routing, so every
	# service other than core-api is unreachable if this names a single service.
	reverse_proxy api-gateway:8000
	tls internal
}
